From 3cb3302fdbefc2cae18159f3348d772a2336de2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab <homelab@emrys.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:56:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] core: enforce the ownership filter server-side, 404 on
 direct access

can_view_snapshot() checks ownership before permissions, so every view that
already asked it now answers for the right user. The direct-URL views
(SnapshotView, SnapshotPathView, the replay hosts, the replay auth handoff)
call require_snapshot_access() explicitly, because a snapshot that is not
yours must answer 404 rather than the private-snapshot login redirect.

Seeing other users' captures is a POST-only, superuser-only session toggle
(/user-scope/see-all/); the admin banner states the active scope. Superusers
are not exempt by default.
---
